  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Huntington Ingalls obligated $2.8B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Huntington Ingalls won 60 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $47.2M. Huntington Ingalls obligations are down 32.4% year over year. Huntington Ingalls remains concentrated in ship-related work: Ship Building and Repairing accounts for $2.7B of FY2026 to date obligations. Huntington Ingalls also recorded obligations in Engineering Services ($58.4M), Other Electronic and Precision Equipment Repair and Maintenance ($39.6M), and Power Boiler and Heat Exchanger Manufacturing ($7.5M). Huntington Ingalls obligations by fiscal year show a multi-year pattern: FY21 $3.6B, FY22 $3B, FY23 $3.2B, FY24 $3.6B, FY25 $4.2B, and FY26 $2.8B. Huntington Ingalls current-year totals are partial, covering fiscal year to date. This snapshot highlights the dominance of ship building and repair in Huntington Ingalls' federal business and the smaller role of non-ship markets in FY2026 to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has Huntington Ingalls' federal business trended recently?",
        "body": "Huntington Ingalls' obligations fell 32.4% year over year. Huntington Ingalls obligated $2.8B in FY2026 to date, down from FY25 $4.2B. Huntington Ingalls totals over the prior five fiscal years were FY21 $3.6B, FY22 $3B, FY23 $3.2B, and FY24 $3.6B, showing variability before the FY25 peak."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What markets drive Huntington Ingalls' federal revenue?",
        "body": "Ship Building and Repairing is the largest market for Huntington Ingalls at $2.7B in FY2026 to date. Huntington Ingalls also has obligations in Engineering Services ($58.4M), Other Electronic and Precision Equipment Repair and Maintenance ($39.6M), and Power Boiler and Heat Exchanger Manufacturing ($7.5M). Huntington Ingalls shows $0 in Hardware Manufacturing for FY2026 to date."
      }
    ]
